// world175:   // WILD1 (2026-10-07, bible/11-Multiplayer/Wild-Zone.md; NOT YET DEPLOYED): THE OPEN ZONE - the `wild` frame (validWildData: the zone's blows and a fallen's gear, routed like a duel's with the sender's verified account; a remains' deposit and its takes, kept by the room - net/wild/wildLaw.js joins the bundle). Deploy the relay first, then the site. Before it, world174: LEGACY7 parts two and three (2026-10-06, bible/06-Systems/Legacy-Arc.md section 9; NOT YET DEPLOYED - world172 on its branch, renumbered past main's WATCH-FIX (world172) and SERPENT3 (world173) at the merge): A HOUSE NAME ONLINE - the identity token may carry the realm character's house (`hn`, `hc`, `hb`, `hg` - net/houseLaw.js, joining the bundle; identityToken.js claimsValid holds them), and the relay stamps it on every row beside the Renown (`badged`; `_named` and the hello's attachment carry it). A relay before it verifies such a token (it ignores claims it does not know) and stamps no house; a service before acct87 signs none (acct85 on its branch, renumbered past main's YARD-SHED and YARD-HEIGHT). TWO PLAYERS WED - the `wed` frame (validWedData, WED_RELAY_MIN), directed like a duel's with the sender's verified account stamped on it - and (AUDIT LEGACY III O1, re-hashed in place) its realm character, `sc`, the identity token's `ci` - on its own meter. Deploy the relay first, then the account service, then the site. Before it, world173: SERPENT3 (2026-10-05, Mac: "the serpent world boss teleports. Nobody has beat it yet."; bible/11-Multiplayer/Sea-Serpent.md section 15; NOT YET DEPLOYED - world171 on its branch, renumbered past main's CRYSTAL-FIST (world171) and then main's WATCH-FIX (world172) at the merges): the relay's serpent brain swims every leg it shows - no leap: a Rising Maw and a coil dashed for under the sea, closed on at the surface first, the Maelstrom formed where it swims, every attack's swim said as it begins, a fight whose room slept taken up circling where it was (serpentResume, before a joiner's state and a word's judging) - and a blow judged where the body lay when it struck; its law's version 2 (SERPENT_BRAIN_MIN: a game before it is told to reload) - and AUDIT SHIPS (2026-10-06, the same release): it leads its marks off each body's pose send time (`ts`, handed on by _serpentBodies), closes no slower than the ship it closes on, counts the ships fighting it by the shares in its health, says every turn of its own SERPENT_SAY_AHEAD_MS ahead, its coil wound and let go so too - the coil frame gains `w`, when its winding is drawn from (a frame without it is drawn from its landing, as before) - takes up a short sleep as it was said and a fight checkpointed by an older law at once, and hears no game it told to reload until it has - and AUDIT SHIPS 2 (2026-10-06, the same release): every steering turn and the closing surge said ahead, a kill between beats unsaying nothing, a coil's round laid about its own centre, the count said on its health's word, a stale game's share out, a ship's send clock held to the relay's (SERPENT_CLOCK_SPAN_MS), and the fight kept before a word that lays its track (serpentSaysTrack). Before it, world172: WATCH-FIX (2026-10-05, Mac: "improve the guards"; bible/06-Systems/Living-World.md WATCH-FIX; NOT YET DEPLOYED): the foe record carries the living-world resident a watchman stands for (`lr`, LIVING_ID_RE) - validFoeRecord admits it, so a relay before it drops it and a reader sees the resident walk beside his own guard, as before. Before it, world171: CRYSTAL-FIST (2026-10-05, the owner, for Flylighter: "Title: Crystal Fist"; NOT YET DEPLOYED - world170 on its branch, renumbered past main's FEUD (world170) at the merge; DEPLOY BEFORE THE ACCOUNT SERVICE'S acct83 - the account deploy waits on this relay's /health, AUDIT B1): the token's vocabulary gains the Crystal Fist's title and glyph (`crystalfist`) and the Crystal Resonance's aura (`resonance`) - src/net/identityToken.js rides the bundle, and a relay before it refuses Flylighter's token from the first one acct83 mints, which carries the glyph whether or not they wear anything (CRYSTAL-FIST AUDIT: this line had the order backwards); no frame changes shape. Before it, world170: FEUD (2026-10-04 and 05, Mac: "Let's do everything in a proper detailed arc"; bible/12-Enhanced-AI/Feud-Arc.md sections 10 and 25; NOT YET DEPLOYED - world162 to world165 on its branch (TELL8, AUDIT TELL, RVN13, FEUD WIRE), one version at its merge of main, renumbered past main's world162-world169): FEUD WIRE (Mac: "Take care of both gaps"; section 25): the foe record carries a revenant's blows (`rb`, its stand's factor per mille) and a wind-up its signature (`wk` +64) - validFoeRecord admits both, so a relay before it drops them. RVN13 (Mac: "more complex, less easy to accomplish and more detailed", then "Go"; section 25): the foe record carries a revenant's adaptations (`ad`), weakness (`wq`), last stand (`p2`) and a band follower's master (`rt`) - validFoeRecord admits them, so a relay before it drops them. AUDIT TELL (Mac: "a comprehensive audit over everything ensuring perfection"): the wind-up record carries its serial (`wn`) and says its landing (`wk` +32), and a hit's blow class is bounded at the heaviest K (1.75) - the relay forwards both unread. TELL8 (Mac: "breath more depth into it", then "Go"; section 10): the foe record carries a wind-up (`wk` `wy` `wl` `wo` `wp`) and a stagger or an overreach (`ws`), and a hit its blow's class (`wc`, hitClassOf) - the relay forwards both unread. Its bundle carries wire.js, and ai/blowShapes.js - AUDIT ARENA-LADDER's leaf - now holds TELL2's numbers, TELL5's family, TELL7's whole set and the verdicts of TELL6's and RVN5's shapes beside the families: the relay's ladder brain asks a kind's family alone (blowShapesOf with no entity), so its fighters throw and are judged as before. Before it, world169: AUDIT ARENA-LADDER (2026-10-05, the owner: "ensure AI enemies sometimes recieve telegraphed attacks, ensure climbing the PvE ladder isnt an easy feat"; bible/01-Overview/audits/Audit-Arena-Ladder.md; NOT YET DEPLOYED - world167 on its branch, renumbered past main's SHADOW-CLOAK (world167) and SERAPH-WINGS (world168) at the merges; DEPLOY AFTER THE ACCOUNT SERVICE'S acct82): THE LADDER IS EARNED ON THE RELAY TOO - a ladder bout's champion is elite (net/arena/arenaLaw.js arenaLadderBout, arenaFoeStats' elite multipliers), the relay's fighters run at the classes' and beasts' own pace, its foes' blows are telegraphed at the player who stands in them (the `atk` word's s/yw/ox/oz, net/arena/arenaBrain.js off ai/blowShapes.js - the leaf joins the bundle), the judges score a time-out as a loss once the fighter is under LADDER_JUDGES_SHARE (systems/arena/arenaBout.js judgesFloor), and the `in` word of a ladder bout must carry the account service's attempt ticket (`z`, ARENA_TICKET_RE) - the relay refuses one without it (an older build's: 'no bout', the word it ends its bout on - AUDIT ARENA-LADDER 2) and signs it into the receipt so the service can match the claim to its attempt, its room and its life (ARENA_ATTEMPT_LIFE_S). AUDIT ARENA-LADDER 2 (undeployed, the same version): one telegraph on the sand at a time, and fighters level on the judges' card a draw. Before it, world167: SHADOW-CLOAK (2026-10-04, the owner, for SirMcMobdon: "A holo shadow cloak with red accents"; NOT YET DEPLOYED - world165 on its branch, renumbered past main's SERPENT1 (world165) and SERPENT2 (world166) at the merges): the token's vocabulary gains the Holo Shadow Cloak's aura (`shadowcloak`, identityToken.js AURAS) - a relay before it refuses SirMcMobdon's token once they wear it (claimsValid); no frame changes shape. Before it, world166: SERPENT2 (2026-10-04, the owner: "the discord integration needs to happen"; bible/11-Multiplayer/Sea-Serpent.md; NOT YET DEPLOYED): THE SERPENT'S HERALD - the hub takes a `serpent` `site` word (SERPENT_KINDS, validSerpentIn - the day, the site's native point to the whole unit and the port it lies off; SERPENT_SITE_RELAY_MIN), keeps the accounts' vote of where it lies (net/gate/gateHerald.js foldGateSite, the gate's law), and posts to the gate's Discord channel off its alarm: the bells fifteen minutes before it rises, pinging SERPENT_DISCORD_ROLE or the gate's role, and the kill at the agreed site alone - a forged site's never (net/serpent/serpentHerald.js joins the bundle; gateHerald.js exports its stamp and list). A relay before it CLOSES the socket on the `site` kind, so the client says it only to world166 or later. Before it, world165: SERPENT1 (2026-10-04, Mac: "A new world event that requires players with a ship to meet up and take on a large scale sea serpent in the ocean"; bible/11-Multiplayer/Sea-Serpent.md; NOT YET DEPLOYED - world162 on its branch, renumbered past main's PRIMARCH (world162) and SUNBABY1 (world163), then world164 past PARTY-LEAD's, at the merges): A NEW FRAME, `serpent` (SERPENT_RELAY_MIN) - a cell room holds Sethrakul's fight when its site stands in it (net/serpent/serpentBrain.js, its beat on the cell's alarm beside the cell's own duties), says it to the sockets about it - every word naming its site, so a client folds its own serpent's alone (AUDIT SERPENT 2 F1) - signs `l1` receipts at the kill (net/serpent/serpentReceipt.js) and tells the hub, which says the kill to everyone online; a relay before it closes the socket on the frame, so no client says one to it. Before it, world164: PARTY-LEAD (2026-10-04, the player: "add a make person party leader option for the leader when in a party"; NOT YET DEPLOYED - world162 on its branch, renumbered past main's PRIMARCH (world162) and SUNBABY1 (world163) at the merge): the hub's `party.lead` act (SOCIAL_ACTS, server/src/index.js _partyLead) - the leader hands the lead to a member who is online, and every member hears the `party.leader` note a leave already says. A relay before it CLOSES the socket on the act (an unknown kind is CLOSE_POLICY), so the