// ═══ WAGONS2-VISIT (2026-10-09, Mac: "People should be able to use the interior just like houses, like crafting and
// such"; who may come in, "Like an online home"): A CARAVAN'S ROOM KEEPS WHAT ITS OWNER PLACED ═══════════════════════
//
// A caravan's room is `caravan:<k>` (net/privateInterior.js caravanRoomOf), `k` its owner's park key - the key the cell's
// record of the parked caravan carries (parkKeyOf, above), so a visitor names the room off the record and the owner
// works it out. What the owner placed in it lives in the owner's save (the caravan's scene), never on any service; so the
// owner says it to the room - `{ t: 'caravan', data: { c, d } }`, `c` the character the frame names (PARK_CHAR_RE, the
// park frame's own) and `d` the room's document (systems/caravanVisit.js caravanDecorDoc: its pieces, unturned, under
// the small frame's cap) or null (nothing kept). The relay reads `c` alone: the frame is the OWNER's only when the
// account its token verified and `c` hash to the room's own key - anyone else's is junk - and the room keeps the last
// document (CARAVAN_DECOR_KEY) until PARK_TTL_MS after it was said (the alarm forgets it; the park record of the caravan
// lives as long), hands it to every joiner after the welcome and fans each new one to whoever is in. So a visit needs no
// owner present: what they placed the last time they stood in their caravan online stands for their visitors.
/** The room's storage key for the document its owner last said. */
export const CARAVAN_DECOR_KEY = 'caravan:decor';
/** WAGONS2-VISIT (AUDIT): the least time between two documents one socket says (ms) - its owner's client says one at
 *  most every 1.5 s (scenes/world.js caravanDecorTick) and once a welcome, a new socket's; a sooner one is dropped. */
export const CARAVAN_DOC_MIN_MS = 1000;
/** The first relay that keeps a caravan's room (the frame - an older relay closes the socket on it). */
export const CARAVAN_RELAY_MIN = 187;
export const relaySupportsCaravan = (v) => { const m = /^world(\d+)$/.exec(typeof v === 'string' ? v : ''); return !!m && Number(m[1]) >= CARAVAN_RELAY_MIN; };
/** A `caravan` frame's data through the door: `{ c, d }` - the character and the document (a plain object, or null to
 *  forget it); the document is the reader's to project (systems/caravanVisit.js readCaravanDecor). Anything else null. */
export function validCaravanData(d) {
  if (!d || typeof d !== 'object' || Array.isArray(d)) return null;
  if (typeof d.c !== 'string' || !PARK_CHAR_RE.test(d.c)) return null;   // the park frame's own character
  if (d.d !== null && (!d.d || typeof d.d !== 'object' || Array.isArray(d.d))) return null;
  return { c: d.c, d: d.d };
}

// ═══ DUEL1 (2026-09-24, Mac: "When inspecting a player, they should be able to send an invite to duel which then traps
// both players in a surrounding transparent holographic wall that keeps them from going outside of the duel space") ═══
//
// THE FIRST FRAME ONE PLAYER'S BLOW RIDES AT ANOTHER. Co-op was never PvP (bible Multiplayer.md): no peer stands in any
// melee, arrow or spell target list, a `hit` names foes alone and a `cast` lands a party mate's gift alone. A duel is
// the one door through that, and it is CONSENSUAL and BOUNDED - two players who both said yes, inside one ring, until
// one of them falls to 1 health (never 0: a duel kills nobody), yields, or it is called off.
//
// ONE DIRECTED FRAME, the card's routing - `{t:'duel', data:{to, k, s, ...}}` from a hello'd socket in a PLACE room to
// the socket `to` names, the sender's id AND its verified account stamped on it by the relay (`sub`, off the identity
// token - the loser's client names the winner's account to the account service by it, so no client's own word says
// whose win it was). The relay reads the SHAPE alone (validDuelData); everything that decides anything is the two
// clients' law (net/duel/duelSession.js):
//   ask / yes / no  the invite (the Inspect card's Challenge) and the answer (the asked player's prompt)
//   start           the asker's word that the duel is ON, and where the ring stands (`c`: the world frame's point -
//                   natives on x and z, metres on y, the pose's own frame). Three steps, so nobody is shut in a ring
//                   the other side never confirmed.
//   cancel          an ask, an answer or a start taken back, with its reason
//   strike          my blow reached my opponent's body: its kind (`by`), where I stood, my weapon, and the damage my own
//                   game rolled (`d`) - INT8 (bible/06-Systems/Integrity-Arc.md): THE RELAY REFEREES IT (net/duel/duelRef.js),
//                   clipped to the weapon my look holds and the arms my token signs; it is routed to nobody. DUEL1's
//                   strike carried my sheet for the DEFENDER to resolve on its own machine - and a defender that never
//                   took a blow never fell.
//   spell           my spell reached my opponent: where I stood and its harm my own game counted (`d`) - the referee's,
//                   three a five seconds, each to sixty (INT10)
//   end             my word that the duel is over for me: `yield`, or a reason (left, dead, cancelled) - the referee
//                   calls it the SENDER's loss once the countdown has run, a cancel before (INT8: `fell` and `draw` are
//                   the referee's to say, never a client's)
